<h2>"Another Snail Planet": A watercolor painting turned animated short</h2> 
<p>After a few stop-motion projects, I found myself limited by the medium. I wanted my scenes to feel otherworldly and whimsical; practically, what I truly wanted was to ground my animations in my watercolors. This was this project’s main motivation: to animate over my paintings. 

<h3>Here's a breakdown of how I transformed a watercolor painting into a 2d animated short:</h3>

<p>First, I digitized an original painting by uploading it on GIMP and removing all snails. This original watercolor painting was inspired by a Crepe Myrtle I met in Atlanta--it's also a part of a painting series, <a href="/projects/tree-at-hansell/"> <i>"The Tree at Hansell St"</i></a>.
</br>


